0. DEFINITIONS

   "The Software" means this software and its accompanying files,
   including source code, documentation and data.

   "The Author" means utomore, the copyright holder.

   "You" means the person or organisation exercising the rights granted
   in section 1.

   "Release" means to publish, distribute, offer for download, sell,
   license, or otherwise make available to anyone other than you or your
   organisation — including as part of a larger work, and including in
   compiled, embedded or otherwise transformed form.

   A "Substantial Portion" of the Software is any part of it whose use
   saves you work you would otherwise have had to do yourself. A handful
   of lines is not; a module, a subsystem, or the design of the interpreter
   is.

1. GRANT

   The Author grants you, free of charge and without royalty, a
   worldwide, non-exclusive, perpetual right to use, study, modify, and
   Release the Software and works derived from it, for any purpose,
   including commercial purposes, subject to sections 2 and 3.

   No trademark rights are granted. This licence says nothing about
   patents.

2. CONDITION — ATTRIBUTION, AND NO CLAIM OF AUTHORSHIP

   You may not present the Software, or a Substantial Portion of it, as
   your own original work. In particular you may not claim authorship of
   it, remove or obscure the copyright notice, relicense it under your own
   name, or state or imply that you created it.

   Anything you Release that contains the Software or a Substantial
   Portion of it must credit the Author by name and identify this project
   as its origin. For software with a user-visible surface — a game, an
   application — placing that credit in the documentation, an about
   screen, or a credits list is sufficient; it need not appear during
   normal use. For source distributions, a copy of this licence file
   alongside the code is sufficient.

   Work you write yourself remains yours, and you may license your own
   contributions as you see fit. This section limits only what you may
   claim about the parts you did not write.

3. CONDITION — NOTIFY THE AUTHOR BEFORE YOU RELEASE

   Before you Release anything containing the Software or a Substantial
   Portion of it, you must notify the Author, by either:

     * opening an issue at
       https://github.com/utomore/particle-magic-system/issues , or
     * sending an email to utomore@outlook.com

   The notice must name the work and say where it can be found.

   This is a notification, not a request for permission. Sending it
   satisfies this section; you do not need a reply and you do not need to
   wait for one.

   Nothing outside a Release requires notice: private use, use inside
   your organisation, evaluation, study, and modifications you never
   Release are all free of this condition.

4. IF YOU BREACH THESE CONDITIONS

   The rights granted in section 1 end automatically if you fail to
   comply with section 2 or section 3. They are reinstated as soon as you
   come into compliance — for section 3, by sending the notice you owed —
   unless the Author notifies you otherwise in writing.

5. NO WARRANTY

   The Software is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. The
   Author makes no promise that it is fit for any purpose, that it works,
   that it is free of defects, or that it does not infringe anyone's
   rights. You bear the entire risk of using it.

6. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

   To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the Author is not
   liable for any claim, damages, loss, or other liability arising from
   the Software or from anything done with it, whether in contract, tort
   or otherwise, and whether or not the Author was advised of the
